  "configuration_id": "config_010",
  "reason": "Evidence: Only one experiment (config_001, RNA-only/PCA/singleprofile) is completed, yielding a low validation accuracy of ~48.5% and F1 of ~46.4%. This gives us a single baseline but leaves the most critical design question unresolved: does the image modality carry complementary signal that could substantially improve performance? Uncertainty: We have no information about image-only performance, so we cannot judge whether multimodal fusion (configs 016–051) is a promising direction or whether the bottleneck lies in the RNA representation/profile choice. What this tests: config_010 (image_only, singleprofile, resnet50) is the minimal, clean counterpart to config_001 on the image side—same singleprofile setting, a standard pretrained encoder—allowing a direct modality comparison. Why it is the best next step: Resolving whether image features are informative at all is the highest-leverage decision for the remaining budget. If image accuracy is markedly higher than 48.5%, we can confidently invest in multimodal configs; if it is similarly low, we should instead focus on improving the RNA pipeline (better encoders, multiprofile aggregation). This single experiment partitions the large remaining search space and avoids committing budget to a modality that may not contribute."
}

